{number: 165}
{title: Give Them All to Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Are you [C] tired of chasing pretty rainbows?
Are you [G7] tired of spinning round and round?
Wrap up [C] all those shattered dreams of your life,
And at the [G7] feet of Jesus lay them [C] down.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Give them [F] all, give them all,
Give them [C] all to Jesus,
Shattered [G7] dreams, wounded hearts, and broken [C] toys;
Give them [F] all, give them all,
Give them [C] all to Jesus,
And He will [G7] turn your sorrows into [C] joy.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
He never [C] said you'd only see sunshine;
He never [G7] said there'd be no rain.
He only [C] promised a heart full of singing,
About the [G7] very things that once brought [C] pain.
{end_of_verse}
